{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A reclaimed worker can merge a pull request while the replacement worker is still checking it, causing a potentially unapproved merge."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A reclaimed worker can push a changed branch while the replacement worker is checking it, interfering with the landing process."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After claim loss, the old worker can record CI outcomes and repair triggers that reflect the actual CI response and are deduplicated."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A stale worker can delete the replacement worker's active checkout, blocking the landing until it is retried."}]}